WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.310
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:16.610
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:25.410
Liar’s Dice | Last player with dice wins
Everyone starts with five dice. Normally you see only your own. This example has two players.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:32.610
A bid estimates the total across every cup, not just your dice. The live total shrinks as players lose dice.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:48.610
Choose quantity and face, then bid
North bids four twos: at least four matching dice across all cups. The opening player cannot challenge.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:52.110
Challenge | Ones are normally wild
East challenges. After the cups open, count twos and wild ones to check whether there are four.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:59.110
Two twos plus two ones make exactly four. The bid is true, so challenger East loses a die.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:08.610
If the count meets the bid, the challenger loses one die; otherwise the bidder loses one. The loser starts the next round and everyone rerolls.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:25.360
Bidding ones removes wilds
Next round East bids three ones. North challenges. This time only actual ones count.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:32.360
There are only two ones. The bid is false, so bidder East loses another die.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:38.610
Once anyone bids ones, ones stop being wild for the rest of that round, even after a different face is bid. A bid of ones counts only ones.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:49.360
Wilds reset with a new round
After rerolling, ones are wild again. East bids three twos and North challenges to check.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:56.610
Four dice match, meeting the bid of three. Challenger North loses a die.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:07.610
Raise quantity or face
North bids one two; East raises to one three. North can challenge if they do not believe it.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:16.610
At the same quantity, faces rank 2,3,4,5,6,1. Alternatively increase quantity and choose any face. After ones, changing face requires more dice. No halving or doubling rule applies.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:52.610
Play to elimination | Repeated rounds accelerated
Each challenge costs one die. Reroll and bid again. Every remaining round is shown here.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:03:02.510
Result | Zero dice means elimination
North loses their final die. East still has three and wins the match.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:32.421
Skip eliminated players. If the loser is eliminated, the next surviving player starts. Later elimination places higher. Return to the room to play again.
